# GENERATED by mvp/scripts/build-audit.mjs from examples/toys/ - edit the
# toy or the spec, then regenerate; tests/audit.test.ts compares.

::p1 [P1: the penguin]: Kern-Isberner's penguin: birds fly at 0.9, penguins are birds at 1, penguins fly at 0.01. Written naively, the low conditional as a 0.01 support, penguins fly at 0.838. As the opposed line, 0.700, the penguin free at 0.057. With the penguin pinned 0.99 the three sentences cannot all hold: penguins fly reads 0.109 and the pin is met at 0.983. The exception as an undercut of birds-fly gives even odds, 0.507; undercut plus rebuttal gives the paper's answer, 0.013; and a fourth rule, birds have beaks, is untouched at 0.948: no drowning.

  # p1a: the low conditional as a 0.01 support, penguin free
  @peng-p1a [Penguin]: free
  @bird-p1a [Bird]: derived
  @fly-p1a [Flies]: derived
  $r1-p1a [Penguins are birds] 1.0 @bird-p1a | @peng-p1a: r1
  $r2-p1a [Birds fly] 0.9 @fly-p1a | @bird-p1a: r2
  $r3-p1a [Penguins fly, weakly] 0.01 @fly-p1a | @peng-p1a: r3 as written in the paper

  # p1b: the low conditional as the opposed line, penguin free
  @peng-p1b [Penguin]: free
  @bird-p1b [Bird]: derived
  @fly-p1b [Flies]: derived
  $r1-p1b [Penguins are birds] 1.0 @bird-p1b | @peng-p1b: r1
  $r2-p1b [Birds fly] 0.9 @fly-p1b | @bird-p1b: r2
  $r3-p1b [Penguins do not fly] 0.99 ~@fly-p1b | @peng-p1b: r3 as the opposed line

  # p1c: the opposed line, penguin pinned 0.99: the three cannot all hold
  @peng-p1c [Penguin] 0.99: pinned, the what-if
  @bird-p1c [Bird]: derived
  @fly-p1c [Flies]: derived
  $r1-p1c [Penguins are birds] 1.0 @bird-p1c | @peng-p1c: r1
  $r2-p1c [Birds fly] 0.9 @fly-p1c | @bird-p1c: r2
  $r3-p1c [Penguins do not fly] 0.99 ~@fly-p1c | @peng-p1c: r3 as the opposed line

  # p1d: the exception as an undercut, penguin pinned
  @peng-p1d [Penguin] 0.99: pinned
  @bird-p1d [Bird]: derived
  @fly-p1d [Flies]: derived
  $r1-p1d [Penguins are birds] 1.0 @bird-p1d | @peng-p1d: r1
  $r2-p1d [Birds fly] 0.9 @fly-p1d | @bird-p1d: r2
  $r3-p1d [Penguins are the exception] 0.99 ~@fly-p1d | @peng-p1d AND $r2-p1d: r3 as the undercut of r2

  # p1e: undercut plus rebuttal, penguin pinned
  @peng-p1e [Penguin] 0.99: pinned
  @bird-p1e [Bird]: derived
  @fly-p1e [Flies]: derived
  $r1-p1e [Penguins are birds] 1.0 @bird-p1e | @peng-p1e: r1
  $r2-p1e [Birds fly] 0.9 @fly-p1e | @bird-p1e: r2
  $r3-p1e [Penguins are the exception] 0.99 ~@fly-p1e | @peng-p1e AND $r2-p1e: r3 as the undercut of r2
  $r3b-p1e [Penguins do not fly] 0.99 ~@fly-p1e | @peng-p1e: r3 as the plain rebuttal, beside the undercut

  # p1f: plus birds have beaks: no drowning
  @peng-p1f [Penguin] 0.99: pinned
  @bird-p1f [Bird]: derived
  @fly-p1f [Flies]: derived
  @beak-p1f [Has a beak]: derived
  $r1-p1f [Penguins are birds] 1.0 @bird-p1f | @peng-p1f: r1
  $r2-p1f [Birds fly] 0.9 @fly-p1f | @bird-p1f: r2
  $r3-p1f [Penguins are the exception] 0.99 ~@fly-p1f | @peng-p1f AND $r2-p1f: r3 as the undercut of r2
  $r3b-p1f [Penguins do not fly] 0.99 ~@fly-p1f | @peng-p1f: r3 as the plain rebuttal
  $e-p1f [Birds have beaks] 0.9 @beak-p1f | @bird-p1f: (e|b), the drowning probe

::p2 [P2: syntax splitting, the independence half]: Two disconnected sub-bases, A supports B at 0.9 and D supports E at 0.8, A pinned 0.99: B reads 0.945 whether D is free at 0.699, pinned 0.99 or denied at 0.010. The independence half of syntax splitting, from block separability.

  # p2a: A pinned 0.99, D free
  @a-p2a [A] 0.99: the antecedent, pinned
  @b-p2a [B]: derived from A
  $ab-p2a [A supports B] 0.9 @b-p2a | @a-p2a: the queried conditional
  @d-p2a [D] 0.7: an unrelated statement in a second block
  @e-p2a [E]: derived from D
  $de-p2a [D supports E] 0.8 @e-p2a | @d-p2a: keeps the second block non-trivial

  # p2b: A and D pinned
  @a-p2b [A] 0.99: the antecedent, pinned
  @b-p2b [B]: derived from A
  $ab-p2b [A supports B] 0.9 @b-p2b | @a-p2b: the queried conditional
  @d-p2b [D] 0.99: the irrelevant conjunct, pinned true
  @e-p2b [E]: derived from D
  $de-p2b [D supports E] 0.8 @e-p2b | @d-p2b: keeps the second block non-trivial

  # p2c: A pinned, D denied
  @a-p2c [A] 0.99: the antecedent, pinned
  @b-p2c [B]: derived from A
  $ab-p2c [A supports B] 0.9 @b-p2c | @a-p2c: the queried conditional
  @d-p2c [D] 0.01: the irrelevant conjunct, pinned false
  @e-p2c [E]: derived from D
  $de-p2c [D supports E] 0.8 @e-p2c | @d-p2c: keeps the second block non-trivial
